{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium","id":1013664,"title":"Dates for the Impergium","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-07T02:56:53-08:00","id":1013664,"title":"Dates for the Impergium","content":"I picked up Shattered Dreams last weekend, but I have only read the first 40 pages. Near as I can tell, the &quot;official&quot; history of the War of Rage begins around 70,000 BCE and ends around 27,000 BCE. Does the book give dates for the Impergium as well? I always put the Impergium much later, because humans don't become enough of a threat to require an Impergium until the Neolithic era at the earliest, but I am curious to see what Onyx Path does with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T05:03:38-08:00","id":1013683,"title":"","content":"The Impergium started some time after ~10,000 BCE according to <i>Shattered Dreams, </i>with this time period lasting 200 generations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T06:32:10-08:00","id":1013717,"title":"","content":"Perfect. That dovetails exactly with my theory. Thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:16:41-08:00","id":1013896,"title":"","content":"The War of Rage extended much longer than your nominated dates in Shattered Dreams - until c. 2000BC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T12:40:15-08:00","id":1013911,"title":"","content":"My understanding from the first 40 pages is that the war ends when the Ananasi, empowered by Queen Ananasa's presence, weave mystical webs of deception to conceal the other Fera from the prying eyes of the Garou. Is this accurate? If so, what is the date for this event?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T13:01:19-08:00","id":1013925,"title":"","content":"That's not the end date of the conflict, as mass killings continue on both sides until c. 2000BC. Shattered Dreams's take on the War of Rage more or less defies a clean start and end date since it's a series of brushfire wars, skirmishes, and larger conflicts that all collectively constitute the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:01:13-08:00","id":1013965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium?p=1013683#post1013683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Impergium started some time after ~10,000 BCE according to <i>Shattered Dreams, </i>with this time period lasting 200 generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd make more sense to start some time before that and continue on longer, given how hard it can be to select for the instinct for The Jibblies. Also, previous sources had it ending before recorded human history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T14:30:12-08:00","id":1013980,"title":"","content":"The dates for the impergium beginning that I have written down are:<br /> 10,000BC (6 sources, with one additional source stating it was already over by this time)<br /> 7,000BC (1 source)<br /> After 3,000BC (1 source, and inferred by reference to the Indus Valley Civilization)<br /> <br /> Dates for the end:<br /> Before 10,000BC (1)<br /> 9500BC (1, inferred from Lepinski Vir)<br /> 7125BC (1)<br /> 7000BC (1)<br /> Before 7000BC (1)<br /> 6000BC (1; inferred from Lepinski Vir)<br /> 4000BC (1)<br /> 2000BC (1)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:31:10-08:00","id":1014047,"title":"","content":"I generally have used 15,000 BP to 10,000 BP as the time frame for the Imperium. I generally have used 20,000 BP to 5,000 BP as the time frame for the War of Rage. Yes, I know Shattered Dreams gives different dates, but I have been using those dates for 20 years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:04:28-08:00","id":1014215,"title":"","content":"In my non-canon view, Shapeshifters killing humans in an organised hunt started being a thing sometime around the Banestorm. After that point the Delirium gradually increased in potency. These hunts were ad-hoc, revenge killings, punishments, warnings, but not the Impergium proper. When Garou formed packs from domesticated wolves, the Impergium ramped up a little bit, as the factions of 'wild' and 'domesticated' formed. When humans started clustering for protection - incidentally developing settlements and agriculture - the Gauntlet around them also thickened noticeably, triggering renewed pogroms, and an easier sell of the idea to even more peacefully inclined shapeshifters. As human populations grew (relatively 'exploded' in areas) and their effects on the Gauntlet, and Caerns and the general environment became pronounced (like with the formation of the first cities) the Impergium (called something else at the time) truly set in.<br /> <br /> Perhaps if the Ratkin had done their job at keeping human populations small, the Garou wouldn't have had to try taking over that role... Perhaps if the changing breeds hadn't ruled humans as deities... but well...<br /> <br /> So this Impergium lasted from around the time of the first cities, for... a long time. Maybe 4000 years, perhaps longer or shorter in specific regions. By the end the Delirium was basically in full effect. Soon after, or around the long tail end's beginning, humans discovered the poison metals. Perhaps this also factored into the Impergium's formal cessation? When the prey can suddenly get righteously pissed off AND wield aggravated damage, calmer, more thoughtful heads can get their wildly progressive views listened to. When human hunting parties start fighting back and killing their wild gods, sometimes those gods' relatives can take a step back and reconsider some attitudes that might make them the next target of human retaliation.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:38:37-08:00","id":1014221,"title":"","content":"Tying into 'oh shit, humans learned how to use gold and silver' notion is a little piece of 'headcanon' I have. Usually I try not to import my unsupported interpretations, but this one seems appropriate.<br /> <br /> If we dig back into changeling, we are told that they gave mankind the gift of silver specifically to kill the Garou with. That's fine and dandy, but it's not as interesting as an alternative reading that incorporates Shattered Dreams and the rise against the Apis of humans with gold. Fiona was the one supposedly responsible for handing man his weapon of choice, and she ties uniquely into the Apis in this alternative interpretation. The Apis manage the breeding of man and beast, selecting mates and marriages for the best fitness. Benevolent apis try and consider the feelings, wants, and desires of their human cattle - but not all apis are benevolent, and some are outright cruel, violent, and tyrannical over their early human wards.<br /> <br /> Enter Fiona, a being literally spawned by the experience of human love. Now watch her, as she grows, see the Apis again and again tear apart human lovers (and human families) because their offspring would be too weak, too impure, or simply impose too much of a strain on the local ecosystem. Imagine the horror and the rage when sees yet another pair of lovers, these ones looking just like those whose fervent and loving coupling spawned her in the intensity of their love, torn from each other's arms, one of them killed for their crime of disobedience, the other exiled to wander alone and scared in the dark night full of wild beasts and cruel watchers. So she decides to help them, and she watches and learns from the Garou and their fera kin, and finally discovers the two things that can let a mortal man fight back with some chance against the horned gods who rule their villages.<br /> <br /> So one night she takes some gold, and she has Dougal forge it into a speartip or a kopesh or a sword or even just a knife. And she goes back and she hands it to one of those lovers who reminds her best of those who spawned her with their dreams of love, and she tells them what to do. And then a horned god dies, drowning in his own blood in the middle of a village he ruled over as a king. And then she does it again, and again, and the idea spreads both through her and through mortal envoys who bring the secret weapon to their kinsmen a valley over, who take it to their old rival across the river so that they can focus on a different enemy, a shared enemy.<br /> <br /> Over time, as the Firstborn morph into the Changelings and the Sidhe, they forget their oldest myths and half-remember others. They forget there ever were Apis, and they never had much reason to arm anyone against the Corax or the Mokole, so they forget that it was gold they first gave man, not silver, and the myth as we're told it in Changeling is born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5307,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","user":"loomer","date":". 12-08-2016, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T02:58:15-08:00","id":1014228,"title":"","content":"Nice!<br /> <br /> I did, at one point, have a tale in SD about a benevolent bull-headed god in a fenced territory asking two brothers to bring gifts to compete for their god's favour. One brother brought a beautiful sparkling yellow rock, the other brought offerings of food. The brothers argued, and then one underwent the first change into a bull-headed god. Seeing their god favour his brother so, the first struck his newly changed brother down with the shining rock.<br /> <br /> Upon seeing this their god exiled the surviving brother from their verdant agricultural land into the harsh and barren wilds beyond, and cursed his children unto the thirteen generation for his crime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T11:20:58-08:00","id":1014389,"title":"","content":"Since the Impergium is supposed to happen because of the rise of agriculture, I can't shake the idea it has to be somewhere around the Neolithic Era. It is really surprising to me to hear interpretations that place it well before agriculture. I think any three thousand year period between 8000 BC to 3000 BC works best. I think that not only must agriculture become established in the Fertile Crescent, but that it has to spread to other area before the Garou - as a whole - can agree to the Impergium.<br /> <br /> I think the Impergium probably began as a local phenomenon with Garou culling local humans as their population increased too much, and it spread informally as agriculture spread and new Garou encountered and learn from other Garou that &quot;This is how we deal with this problem here.&quot; Whatever concolation &quot;started&quot; the Impergium was probably just the time when the policy became formalized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium?p=1014221#post1014221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we dig back into changeling, we are told that they gave mankind the gift of silver specifically to kill the Garou with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did not know that. That is interesting. When supposedly did this happen? I'm assuming that the best match is with the discovery of silver mining which brings us back to the Neolithic times and therefore the Impergium. I'm sure there is a good story in there. Most likely the Garou killed some human that the local Fae really liked (I imagine some mortal loving a Sidhe) and this was done as punishment for the affront.<br /> <br /> If this story is known in Changeling and not in Werewolf, then it means that this must not be popularly known or believed by the Garou otherwise it would have much more notoriety.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:05:01-08:00","id":1014407,"title":"","content":"sometime after the fall of the drachid and rise of humanity, and before the construction of the pyramids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T12:06:42-08:00","id":1014408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium?p=1014389#post1014389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Impergium is supposed to happen because of the rise of agriculture, I can't shake the idea it has to be somewhere around the Neolithic Era. It is really surprising to me to hear interpretations that place it well before agriculture. I think any three thousand year period between 8000 BC to 3000 BC works best. I think that not only must agriculture become established in the Fertile Crescent, but that it has to spread to other area before the Garou - as a whole - can agree to the Impergium.<br /> <br /> I think the Impergium probably began as a local phenomenon with Garou culling local humans as their population increased too much, and it spread informally as agriculture spread and new Garou encountered and learn from other Garou that &quot;This is how we deal with this problem here.&quot; Whatever concolation &quot;started&quot; the Impergium was probably just the time when the policy became formalized.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I did not know that. That is interesting. When supposedly did this happen? I'm assuming that the best match is with the discovery of silver mining which brings us back to the Neolithic times and therefore the Impergium. I'm sure there is a good story in there. Most likely the Garou killed some human that the local Fae really liked (I imagine some mortal loving a Sidhe) and this was done as punishment for the affront.<br /> <br /> If this story is known in Changeling and not in Werewolf, then it means that this must not be popularly known or believed by the Garou otherwise it would have much more notoriety.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't give a specific date, other than being during the impergium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T16:30:59-08:00","id":1014509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium?p=1014389#post1014389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Impergium is supposed to happen because of the rise of agriculture,</div> </div> </div> </div>Humans don't need agriculture to expand beyond their original bounds and upset other locales, though; it just makes the problem worse. Ratkin may have eaten grain as humans began growing and stockpiling it in massive amounts, but earlier on, they were probably keeping humans from their kills or gnawing spear hafts up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-08T21:16:58-08:00","id":1014608,"title":"","content":"Well, hunter-gatherer populations were probably controlled by low birth rates (caused by low carbohydrate diets and highly athletic physiques) and high fatality rates (large carnivores and large herbivores can be dangerous). I imagine that the Ratkin tended to winnow human populations when climate changes suddenly increased population density above the local sustainable level, which would range from 1 person per square mile in barren deserts to 10 people per square mile in fertile marshes. Otherwise, I imagine that the Ratkin would keep to the margins of human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T03:06:11-08:00","id":1014669,"title":"","content":"Loomer: Wow! I also use the idea that the Fae, specifically Fiona and Dougal, gave humans the secrets of crafting silver and gold weapons, which in turn leads to the end of the Impergium. What do you think of the role of the Weaver in ending the Impergium?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T07:15:01-08:00","id":1014747,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, silver was rarer than gold in the Old World before the discovery of lead. The silver mines that made Athens wealthy were actually lead mines, it was just that the silver byproduct of the lead mining was much more valuable by weight than the lead product. Before the discovery of lead, silver was found in small amounts in copper and gold mines, but, unlike copper and gold, it was rarely found in native form. During the Neolithic era, silver would have likely been much rarer than gold and, because of its high melting temperature, would have been harder to work. Of course, this does not apply to the New World, where there were practically mountains made of silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T05:51:51-08:00","id":1015650,"title":"","content":"Good news! The date given for the start of the Impergium in Shattered Dreams is around 10,000 BCE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T04:17:49-08:00","id":1016486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1013664-dates-for-the-impergium?p=1015650#post1015650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good news! The date given for the start of the Impergium in Shattered Dreams is around 10,000 BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>As per post #2 of this thread...<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}